### 16:40–17:00 · Nói to có ghi âm — 3 phút

> **1. What I did**
> *"This was the hardest week so far. I wrote a TurboModule from scratch — TypeScript spec, Codegen, Kotlin on Android, and Swift behind an Objective-C++ bridge on iOS. Then I rebuilt the same module with the Expo Modules API in about a third of the code."*
>
> **2. What I actually learned**
> *"The thing I'll remember is proving lazy loading myself rather than reading about it. I put a log in the module constructor, launched the app, and nothing fired until I opened the screen that uses it. That's a much better answer in an interview than repeating a definition."*
>
> **3. What was hardest**
> *"The iOS side. Swift can't subclass the generated C++ class, so you need an Objective-C++ file in between, and I lost most of a morning to the Swift header name. ___"*
>
> **4. Next week**
> *"Next week is performance — profiling, Hermes, bundle size. I want a second measured before-and-after story to go alongside the FlashList numbers."*

